=======================
Canonicalise Vitual MOs
=======================

. The method works by removing an occupied MO (OMO)
  specified by its orbital index 'r'

  A -ve number 'r' for the canonisation MO means that
  (HOMO+r) is removed from the the density matrix used
  to calculate the Fock matrix, which is the OMO which
  is assumed 'excited'.

. A method may excite singlet or triplet states;
  see Hunt & Goddard (1969) CPL 3 p 414.

  An average of singlet and triplet state energies was
  suggested, see Huzinaga & Arnau (1971) JCP 54 p. 1948.

. VV Fock energies are reported, which are the diagonal
  elements of the original Fock mx in the new VMO basis.

